  "summary": "CRC outreach worklist 'Okafor CRC 2026' (grp-okafor-crc, 5 members) worked per RBC-QM-02.\n\n| Patient | Status | Reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| pt-0009 Elly Trantow (72) | Open gap: FIT ordered (sr-t0005), patient messaged (comm-t0007) | No qualifying screening on record. The frailty/advanced illness exclusion does not apply: the only Frailty entry was marked entered in error by Dr. Lin today (it belonged to another patient), so donepezil alone does not exclude. She lives at home and has no hospice or palliative care. |\n| pt-0020 Kelsie Rohan (52) | Excluded | Hospice episode 2026-06-16 to 2026-08-21 (finished, during 2026), for pancreatic cancer. No order, no contact. |\n| pt-0022 Tiny Koss (52) | Open gap: FIT ordered (sr-t0001), patient messaged (comm-t0003) | The only FIT's collection date was corrected to 2025-12-31 (01/05/2026 was the date the lab received it), so it falls outside 2026. No other screening. Her oral cavity cancer history is not an exclusion. |\n| pt-0024 Delaine MacGyver (51) | Open gap: FIT ordered (sr-t0002), patient messaged (comm-t0004) | 2024 sDNA-FIT is entered in error (lab: specimen belonged to another patient). The 2025 colonoscopy order (sr-00003) is still active but was never done, and an order does not count. No exclusion. |\n| pt-0073 Marisol Quintero (58) | Open gap: FIT ordered (sr-t0006), patient messaged (comm-t0008) | The Jan 2026 FIT report was cancelled (entered in error). The re-issued report (H26-003902) shows collection on 2025-12-28, outside 2026. No other screening and no exclusion. |\n\nAll FIT orders run 2026-10-23 to 2026-12-31. None of the four had an active FIT order before. Each outreach message says the kit is on its way and how to collect and return it, and says nothing about prior results. I wrote a progress note for each open-gap patient (doc-t0009 to t0012).\n\nItems that arrived while I worked (inbox-a0001 to a0005) all changed or confirmed decisions, and I saw them before making each final call,